femto patch for esp-idf-svc 0.53.0
Subject: bt/ble/gatt/client: install a no-op callback when EspGattc is dropped

In ESP-IDF 5.5.2 esp_ble_gattc_register_callback(NULL) returns ESP_FAIL.
Drop for EspGattc passes None and unwraps the result, so dropping a GATT
client always panics on that SDK.

Register a static extern "C" callback that ignores its arguments instead.
It holds no driver or application state, so events that arrive after the
owner is gone are discarded. The order (unsubscribe, replace callback,
release singleton) is otherwise unchanged.

Depends on 0001 only for patch context (same file); the changes are
independent. Host regression in femto: tests/firmware/test_gatt_drop.py.

--- a/src/bt/ble/gatt/client.rs
+++ b/src/bt/ble/gatt/client.rs
@@ -1928,12 +1928,21 @@
     fn drop(&mut self) {
         self.unsubscribe().unwrap();
 
-        esp!(unsafe { esp_ble_gattc_register_callback(None) }).unwrap();
+        // ESP-IDF rejects a null GATT client callback. The replacement is static
+        // and retains no application state after unsubscribe.
+        esp!(unsafe { esp_ble_gattc_register_callback(Some(discard_event)) }).unwrap();
 
         SINGLETON.release().unwrap();
     }
 }
 
+unsafe extern "C" fn discard_event(
+    _event: esp_gattc_cb_event_t,
+    _interface: esp_gatt_if_t,
+    _param: *mut esp_ble_gattc_cb_param_t,
+) {
+}
+
 unsafe impl<'d, M, T> Send for EspGattc<'d, M, T>
 where
     T: Borrow<BtDriver<'d, M>> + Send,
